cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this authenticator, please cite the paper below."
title: "ZT-Authenticator: a device- and relying-party-bound signing authenticator"
abstract: >-
  A research authenticator that binds every approval to the enrolled device key
  and to the relying party. It renders and signs the canonical intent on one
  device, and is the second signing backend evaluated in the Proof-of-Intent
  Authorization (PoIA) work.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ztn-iplab/ZT-Authenticator"
